   "subject": "Why elements of x-axis are sorted?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi,\r<br>\r<br>Here I have following plot :\r<br>\r<br>set.seed(100)\r<br>df1 &lt;- data.frame(Q = c(rep(NA, 2), rnorm(22)),\r<br>                        Q1 = rep(sample(letters, 12), 2),\r<br>                        Q2 =  paste(&quot;AA&quot;, rep(1:2, each=12), sep=&quot;-&quot;))\r<br>df1\r<br>ggplot(df1) +\r<br>          geom_line(aes(y=Q, x=Q1, group=Q2, colour=Q2))\r<br>\r<br>Looking at the x-axis, it seems that ggplot sorts the elements of the\r<br>&quot;Q1&quot; and then plots. How to force ggplot to keep the same order as it\r<br>is originally?\r<br>\r<br>Thanks,\r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.\r<br>Please provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"http://gist.github.com/270442\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gist.github.com/270442&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383284049000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38V3ksKOcy_SaHDCqVcdna\">http://gist.github.com/270442</a>\r<br>\r<br>To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383284049000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0C2sdA1lXOSIMerAQhwgvH\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
