    [
     1,
     "I remembered looking into this before and found this old thread from the group...<div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/browse_thread/thread/e3972ce2faee3ada/2bc943f31376c550?lnk=gst&amp;q=axis+labels#2bc943f31376c550\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/browse_thread/thread/e3972ce2faee3ada/2bc943f31376c550?lnk%3Dgst%26q%3Daxis%2Blabels%232bc943f31376c550&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383284050000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08mfaNGagswEQlSMifk0MA\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/browse_thread/thread/e3972ce2faee3ada/2bc943f31376c550?lnk=gst&amp;q=axis+labels#2bc943f31376c550</a></div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Wherein there is a link to Nabble: </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/ggplot-boxplot-how-to-order-categories-td835093.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/ggplot-boxplot-how-to-order-categories-td835093.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383284050000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-zWb9kzdPC6u_f9_mJ7NP\">http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/ggplot-boxplot-how-to-order-categories-td835093.html</a></div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Wherein Hadley Says the following:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,geneva,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse\"><span>Hi Raj,</span><br>\r\n\r\n<br><span>It&#39;s the same as the other plotting systems in R: you need <b style=\"background-image:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-color:rgb(255,255,102);background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">to</b> change</span><br>\r\n\r\n<span>the <b style=\"background-image:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-color:rgb(255,255,102);background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">order</b> of the underlying factor levels.  e.g.:</span><br>\r\n\r\n<br><span>levels(diamonds$color) &lt;- c(&quot;J&quot;, &quot;D&quot;, &quot;E&quot;, &quot;I&quot;, &quot;H&quot;, &quot;F&quot;, &quot;G&quot;)</span><br><br><span>If you&#39;re reordering then according <b style=\"background-image:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-color:rgb(255,255,102);background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">to</b> the value of another variable,</span><br>\r\n\r\n<span>also see ?reorder</span><br><br><span>Hadley</span><br>--------------------------------------------</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,geneva,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse\"><br>\r\n\r\n</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,geneva,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse\">Looks like you need to create a list of your variables in the order that you want them on the graph and then plot according to that. </span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,geneva,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,geneva,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse\">HTH,</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,geneva,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,geneva,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse\">Brandon</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,geneva,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse\"><br><div style=\"border-top-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-right-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-bottom-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);overflow-x:hidden;overflow-y:hidden;min-height:160px\">\r\n\r\n<font face=\"arial\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;font-size:small\">P.S. Nice example, worked like a charm.</span></font></div></span></div>"
